module : spocq/gensrc/mcp/test/  — run-all.sh (the 23 numbered scripts),
         shakedown.sh (requirement-keyed, with a coverage roll-up),
         mcp-selftest.lisp (in the image, via execute-spocq)
run    : cd spocq/gensrc/mcp/test
         STORE_HOST=https://nl4.dydra.com STORE_TOKEN=<token> \
           MCP_PATH=/test/test/mcp MCP_INSECURE=1 ./run-all.sh
         MCP_URL=<url> MCP_TOKEN=<token> ./shakedown.sh
needs  : a live MCP endpoint AND A VALID TOKEN. common.sh carries a
         default STORE_TOKEN for localhost; nl4 does not accept it.
         Override it from the environment and REDACT tokens from any log
         copied in here — the record names hosts and accounts, never a token.
output : shakedown writes results/<UTC date>-<account>-<repo>.log; each
         check carries an id that appears on every line it produced, so
         one check reads end to end with  grep '\[12\]' results/<log>
